From: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia.pukngae@linux.dev>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:18:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: hci_qca: Accept wake ACKs while IBS is disabled

Piano wakes the UART controller during setup, before starting the in-band
sleep state machine. The resulting ACK arrives while the transmit state
is ASLEEP, where the driver reports a protocol error.

Ignore an ACK in this state while IBS is disabled. Preserve the usual
diagnostic after runtime IBS negotiation and leave WAKING unchanged.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia.pukngae@linux.dev>
---
 drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c
index 3e921e197..366720f92 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c
@@ -892,6 +892,10 @@ static void device_woke_up(struct hci_uart *hu)
 		break;
 
 	case HCI_IBS_TX_ASLEEP:
+		/* Setup may wake the controller before enabling runtime IBS. */
+		if (test_bit(QCA_IBS_DISABLED, &qca->flags))
+			break;
+		fallthrough;
 	default:
 		BT_ERR("Received HCI_IBS_WAKE_ACK in tx state %d",
 		       qca->tx_ibs_state);
